          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AsciiDoc.py always drops the line that contains a reference to a missing attribute (effectively "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "attribute-missing=drop-line"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). This “feature” was a side effect of how the processor was implemented and not designed with the writer in mind. The behavior is frustrating for the writer because it’s hard to detect where its occurring and can result in loss of important content. That’s why Asciidoctor uses a different default behavior and, further, allows the behavior to be customized."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "History"
              }
            ],
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "There are a few cases where the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "attribute-missing"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute is not strictly honored. One of those cases is the include directive. If a missing attribute is found in the target of an include directive, the processor will issue a warning about the missing attribute and leave behind the same warning message in the converted document."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Another case is the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ifeval"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " directive. A missing attribute reference can safely be used in the clause of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ifeval"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " directive without any side effects (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "drop"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") since the purpose of that statement is to determine whether an attribute resolves to a value."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If you want the processor to fail when the document contains a missing attribute, set the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "attribute-missing"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " attribute to "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "warn"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " and pass the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "--failure-level=WARN"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " option to the CLI."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "literal",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "$ asciidoctor -a attribute-missing=warn --failure-level=WARN doc.adoc"
                  }
                ],
                "language": null,
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The processor will convert the entire document, but the application will complete with a non-zero exit status."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "When using the API, you can consult the logger for the max severity of all messages reported or look for specific messages in the stack. It’s up to the application code to decide how and when to terminate the application."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
